    "id": "reformed-cessationist-pattern",
    "q": "Why do many Calvinist, Calvinist-leaning and cessationist voices seem to do more exposing? What teachings and dynamics contribute, and is the pattern fair to assume?",
    "short": "There is a visible pattern online, and some teachings make polemics feel natural in these circles: a strong stress on doctrinal precision, a long tradition of confessional debate, and (for cessationists) the belief that modern miracle and prophecy claims cannot be genuine. But it is a pattern of ideas and incentives, not a verdict on people. Other camps do the same, and many Reformed and cessationist Christians reject harsh call-out culture.",
