          "That impression is understandable, but impressions are not data. We notice the loudest voices, algorithms show us more of what provokes us, and we rarely see the quiet Reformed pastor who spends his week visiting the sick. So it is wise to talk about patterns in teaching and incentives, and to be slow to judge any group, let alone any person."
