          "<strong>A polemical heritage.</strong> The Reformers wrote fierce polemics (Luther’s invective is famous), and church history includes much darker moments, such as Geneva’s execution of Michael Servetus in 1553. Many Reformed Christians today openly lament that history. <strong>Online dynamics</strong> then amplify everything: the “Young, Restless, Reformed” movement of the 2000s grew up alongside blogs, podcasts and YouTube, where sharp critique travels fast."
