          "From the relational view, the deeper issue is not Calvinism or cessationism as such, but any framing in which God is mainly a guardian of correct information and salvation hangs on getting every doctrine right. Then error becomes terrifying and must be policed. When the gospel is first God’s self-giving union with us in Christ, we can still care deeply about truth, but we hold it the way Jesus held it: “full of grace and truth” (John 1:14)."
