          "Paul says that even perfect knowledge and the faith to move mountains, without love, are “nothing” (1 Cor 13:2). The Greek word <em>agapē</em> here describes a love that is patient, kind, not proud and not keeping score (1 Cor 13:4-5). It is the love God has shown us in Christ (Rom 5:8)."
